	 (263,'alpha_vantage','CART','CART','2026-02-01 18:01:21','20260201T180121','Instacart Brass In Hot Seat As Shareholder Probe Follows FTC Price Games','https://hoodline.com/2026/02/instacart-brass-in-hot-seat-as-shareholder-probe-follows-ftc-price-games/','Instacart''s parent company, Maplebear Inc., is under investigation by securities law firm Kahn Swick & Foti, LLC, for potential breaches of fiduciary duty and legal violations. This shareholder probe follows a $60 million settlement with the Federal Trade Commission over deceptive advertising and problematic refund practices, and scrutiny regarding Instacart''s use of an AI pricing tool that led to significant price variations for consumers. Instacart has since halted item-level price testing and pledged to align online and in-store pricing.','https://img.hoodline.com/2026/2/instacart-brass-in-hot-seat-as-shareholder-probe-follows-ftc-price-games-2.webp?max-h=442&w=760&fit=crop&crop=faces,center','Hoodline','General','Hoodline','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.943376"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.807015"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.716250"}]',-0.460748,'Bearish','[{"ticker": "CART", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.498090"}]','{"url": "https://hoodline.com/2026/02/instacart-brass-in-hot-seat-as-shareholder-probe-follows-ftc-price-games/", "title": "Instacart Brass In Hot Seat As Shareholder Probe Follows FTC Price Games", "source": "Hoodline", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.943376"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.807015"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.716250"}], "authors": ["Emily Johnson"], "summary": "Instacart''s parent company, Maplebear Inc., is under investigation by securities law firm Kahn Swick & Foti, LLC, for potential breaches of fiduciary duty and legal violations. This shareholder probe follows a $60 million settlement with the Federal Trade Commission over deceptive advertising and problematic refund practices, and scrutiny regarding Instacart''s use of an AI pricing tool that led to significant price variations for consumers. Instacart has since halted item-level price testing and pledged to align online and in-store pricing.", "banner_image": "https://img.hoodline.com/2026/2/instacart-brass-in-hot-seat-as-shareholder-probe-follows-ftc-price-games-2.webp?max-h=442&w=760&fit=crop&crop=faces,center", "source_domain": "Hoodline", "time_published": "20260201T180121", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "CART", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.498090"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bearish", "overall_sentiment_score": -0.460748}','2026-02-02 06:39:59',NULL),
	 (264,'alpha_vantage','CFR','CFR','2026-02-01 11:51:25','20260201T115125','New York State Common Retirement Fund Raises Holdings in Cullen/Frost Bankers, Inc. $CFR','https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-new-york-state-common-retirement-fund-raises-holdings-in-cullenfrost-bankers-inc-cfr-2026-02-01/','The New York State Common Retirement Fund increased its stake in Cullen/Frost Bankers, Inc. (NYSE:CFR) by 45.9% during the third quarter, now owning 189,200 shares valued at $23,985,000. Several other institutional investors also adjusted their positions in CFR, with a significant amount of the company''s stock, 86.90%, held by institutional investors and hedge funds. Analysts currently have a "Hold" consensus rating on the stock with a target price of $138.18, following recent positive Q4 earnings results and increased dividend announcements.','https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/cullen-frost-logo-1200x675.jpg','MarketBeat','General','MarketBeat','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.938529"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.832303"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.818111"}]',0.498009,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "CFR", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.483295"}]','{"url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-new-york-state-common-retirement-fund-raises-holdings-in-cullenfrost-bankers-inc-cfr-2026-02-01/", "title": "New York State Common Retirement Fund Raises Holdings in Cullen/Frost Bankers, Inc. $CFR", "source": "MarketBeat", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.938529"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.832303"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.818111"}], "authors": ["MarketBeat"], "summary": "The New York State Common Retirement Fund increased its stake in Cullen/Frost Bankers, Inc. (NYSE:CFR) by 45.9% during the third quarter, now owning 189,200 shares valued at $23,985,000. Several other institutional investors also adjusted their positions in CFR, with a significant amount of the company''s stock, 86.90%, held by institutional investors and hedge funds. Analysts currently have a \\"Hold\\" consensus rating on the stock with a target price of $138.18, following recent positive Q4 earnings results and increased dividend announcements.", "banner_image": "https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/cullen-frost-logo-1200x675.jpg", "source_domain": "MarketBeat", "time_published": "20260201T115125", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "CFR", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.483295"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.498009}','2026-02-02 06:40:03',NULL),
	 (265,'alpha_vantage','CL','CL','2026-02-02 06:06:00','20260202T060600','Colgate-Palmolive reports full-year 2025 sales growth as impairment weighs on GAAP earnings','https://www.globalcosmeticsnews.com/colgate-palmolive-reports-full-year-2025-sales-growth-as-impairment-weighs-on-gaap-earnings/','Colgate-Palmolive announced modest sales growth for full-year 2025, with net sales increasing 1.4% to US$20.382 billion. However, GAAP earnings per share saw a significant 25% decline, largely due to a US$794 million impairment charge related to its skin health business, particularly due to underperformance in China. Despite these GAAP losses, the company exhibited strong cash generation, returning US$2.9 billion to shareholders, and plans to focus on organic growth through science-led innovation in its updated 2026 guidance and 2030 strategy.','https://www.globalcosmeticsnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/colgate-clock-sunset.jpg','Global Cosmetics News','General','Global Cosmetics News','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.912400"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.833174"}]',-0.279471,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "CL", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.299293"}]','{"url": "https://www.globalcosmeticsnews.com/colgate-palmolive-reports-full-year-2025-sales-growth-as-impairment-weighs-on-gaap-earnings/", "title": "Colgate-Palmolive reports full-year 2025 sales growth as impairment weighs on GAAP earnings", "source": "Global Cosmetics News", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.912400"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.833174"}], "authors": ["Global Cosmetics News"], "summary": "Colgate-Palmolive announced modest sales growth for full-year 2025, with net sales increasing 1.4% to US$20.382 billion. However, GAAP earnings per share saw a significant 25% decline, largely due to a US$794 million impairment charge related to its skin health business, particularly due to underperformance in China. Despite these GAAP losses, the company exhibited strong cash generation, returning US$2.9 billion to shareholders, and plans to focus on organic growth through science-led innovation in its updated 2026 guidance and 2030 strategy.", "banner_image": "https://www.globalcosmeticsnews.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/colgate-clock-sunset.jpg", "source_domain": "Global Cosmetics News", "time_published": "20260202T060600", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "CL", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.299293"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "overall_sentiment_score": -0.279471}','2026-02-02 06:40:07',NULL),
	 (266,'alpha_vantage','CL','CL','2026-02-02 03:57:19','20260202T035719','Earnings To Watch: Clorox (CLX) Reports Q4 Results Tomorrow','https://finviz.com/news/294903/earnings-to-watch-clorox-clx-reports-q4-results-tomorrow','Clorox (CLX) is set to report its Q4 results after market hours this Tuesday. Analysts expect a 2.6% year-on-year revenue decline to $1.64 billion and adjusted earnings of $1.43 per share. The company beat revenue expectations last quarter, and its peers like Colgate-Palmolive and Procter & Gamble have shown positive revenue growth in their recent Q4 reports.','https://news-assets.stockstory.org/cover-images/_1400x700_crop_center-center_none/clorox-cover-image-6bc0b517799c_2023-11-09-104758_mtbu.jpeg','Finviz','General','Finviz','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.918948"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.727852"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.633821"}]',0.193449,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.278016"}, {"ticker": "PG", "relevance_score": "0.630480", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.108773"}, {"ticker": "CL", "relevance_score": "0.609170", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.211763"}]','{"url": "https://finviz.com/news/294903/earnings-to-watch-clorox-clx-reports-q4-results-tomorrow", "title": "Earnings To Watch: Clorox (CLX) Reports Q4 Results Tomorrow", "source": "Finviz", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.918948"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.727852"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.633821"}], "authors": ["Anthony Lee"], "summary": "Clorox (CLX) is set to report its Q4 results after market hours this Tuesday. Analysts expect a 2.6% year-on-year revenue decline to $1.64 billion and adjusted earnings of $1.43 per share. The company beat revenu