	 (464,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-02 19:41:39','20260202T194139','HR executive claims Amazon, Whole Foods fired her after bias complaint','https://www.hcamag.com/us/specialization/diversity-inclusion/hr-executive-claims-amazon-whole-foods-fired-her-after-bias-complaint/563957','A Black HR executive, Virginia LaChon, has filed a federal lawsuit against Amazon and Whole Foods, alleging she was fired shortly after complaining about discrimination and while on medical leave. LaChon claims she was subjected to an atypical reporting structure and faced heightened scrutiny compared to non-BIPOC counterparts, leading to a discrimination charge and subsequent termination. The lawsuit seeks various damages and a jury trial, raising questions about reporting structures, treatment of employees on leave, and the timing of investigations.','https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cdn-cgi/image/w=1000,h=600,f=auto/https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cms/images/us/035/0356_639056578254372497.jpg','HRD America','General','HRD America','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.846156"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.642043"}]',-0.335261,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.987890", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.331863"}]','{"url": "https://www.hcamag.com/us/specialization/diversity-inclusion/hr-executive-claims-amazon-whole-foods-fired-her-after-bias-complaint/563957", "title": "HR executive claims Amazon, Whole Foods fired her after bias complaint", "source": "HRD America", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.846156"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.642043"}], "authors": ["Tez Romero"], "summary": "A Black HR executive, Virginia LaChon, has filed a federal lawsuit against Amazon and Whole Foods, alleging she was fired shortly after complaining about discrimination and while on medical leave. LaChon claims she was subjected to an atypical reporting structure and faced heightened scrutiny compared to non-BIPOC counterparts, leading to a discrimination charge and subsequent termination. The lawsuit seeks various damages and a jury trial, raising questions about reporting structures, treatment of employees on leave, and the timing of investigations.", "banner_image": "https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cdn-cgi/image/w=1000,h=600,f=auto/https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cms/images/us/035/0356_639056578254372497.jpg", "source_domain": "HRD America", "time_published": "20260202T194139", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.987890", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.331863"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "overall_sentiment_score": -0.335261}','2026-02-03 13:43:44',NULL),
	 (465,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-02 19:36:39','20260202T193639','Amazon worker lawsuit alleges mishandling of disability leave and firing','https://www.hcamag.com/us/specialization/employment-law/amazon-worker-lawsuit-alleges-mishandling-of-disability-leave-and-firing/563956','A former Amazon warehouse worker, Maria Banuelos, has filed a lawsuit against Amazon.com Services, LLC, alleging disability discrimination, FMLA interference, and retaliation. Banuelos claims Amazon mishandled her disability accommodations and fired her after she requested medical leave for complications from foot surgeries, despite initially approving some accommodations. The lawsuit highlights potential gaps between corporate accommodation policies and their implementation by managers.','https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cdn-cgi/image/w=1000,h=600,f=auto/https://cdn-res.keymedia.com/cms/images/us/035/0356_639056576448278082.jpg','HRD America','General','HRD America','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.822122"}, {"topic": "life_sciences", "relevance_score": "0.642834"}]',-0.645082,'Bearish','[{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.626939"}]','{"url": "https://www.hcamag.com/us/specialization/employment-law/amazon-worker-lawsuit-alleges-mishandling-of-disability-leave-and-firing/563956", "title": "Amazon worker lawsuit alleges mishandling of disability leave and firing", "source": "HRD America", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.822122"}, {"topic": "life_sciences", "relevance_score": "0.642834"}], "authors": ["Tez Romero"], "summary": "A former Amazon warehouse worker, Maria Banuelos, has filed a lawsuit against Amazon.com Services, LLC, alleging disability discrimination, FMLA interference, and retaliation. Banuelos claims Amazon mishandled her disability accommodations and fired her after she requested medical leave for complications from foot surgeries, despit