	 (662,'alpha_vantage','KR','KR','2026-02-02 19:58:25','20260202T195825','How Investors May Respond To Weis Markets (WMK) Declining ROCE And Mature Capital Deployment Profile','https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-retailing/nyse-wmk/weis-markets/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-weis-markets-wmk-declining-roce','Weis Markets (WMK) has seen its Return on Capital Employed (ROCE) decline to 7.2% over the past five years, now trailing the Consumer Retailing industry average. This indicates a mature business with limited opportunities for high-return reinvestment. The article suggests that future performance will likely depend on margin resilience, cost control, and capital allocation, rather than significant growth, advising investors to consider capital efficiency closely.',NULL,'Simply Wall Street','General','Simply Wall Street','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.917686"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.848385"}]',-0.173091,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "WMK", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.291081"}, {"ticker": "KR", "relevance_score": "0.647914", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.045231"}]','{"url": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-retailing/nyse-wmk/weis-markets/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-weis-markets-wmk-declining-roce", "title": "How Investors May Respond To Weis Markets (WMK) Declining ROCE And Mature Capital Deployment Profile", "source": "Simply Wall Street", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.917686"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.848385"}], "authors": ["Simply Wall St"], "summary": "Weis Markets (WMK) has seen its Return on Capital Employed (ROCE) decline to 7.2% over the past five years, now trailing the Consumer Retailing industry average. This indicates a mature business with limited opportunities for high-return reinvestment. The article suggests that fu