	 (781,'alpha_vantage','TGT','TGT','2026-02-02 19:28:00','20260202T192800','Target Corporation (TGT): A Bull Case Theory','https://www.insidermonkey.com/blog/target-corporation-tgt-a-bull-case-theory-7-1669709/','This article summarizes a bullish thesis on Target Corporation (TGT) by David J. Waldron, emphasizing the retailer''s stable dividend profile and consistent owners'' earnings for investors seeking reliable yields and capital gains. Target is presented as a stable company with predictable dividend payments and moderate growth, despite its "none" moat rating from Morningstar and underperformance against the S&P 500 in revenue growth. The thesis highlights Target''s strong in-person presence and its strategy combining brick-and-mortar retail with local store-driven online fulfillment.','https://imonkey-blog.imgix.net/blog/wp-content/uploads/2015/05/supermarket-507295_1280.jpg?auto=format&fit=clip&expires=1801612800&width=480&height=357','Insider Monkey','General','Insider Monkey','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.935125"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.828464"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.746332"}]',0.308148,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.309818"}]','{"url": "https://www.insidermonkey.com/blog/target-corporation-tgt-a-bull-case-theory-7-1669709/", "title": "Target Corporation (TGT): A Bull Case Theory", "source": "Insider Monkey", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.935125"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.828464"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.746332"}], "authors": ["Ricardo Pillai"], "summary": "This article summarizes a bullish thesis on Target Corporation (TGT) by David J. Waldron, emphasizing the retailer''s stable dividend profile and consistent owners'' earnings for investors seeking reliable yields and capital gains. T