	 (786,'alpha_vantage','TGT','TGT','2026-02-02 15:46:29','20260202T154629','New Target CEO Outlines 4 Priorities for Next Chapter','https://progressivegrocer.com/new-target-ceo-outlines-4-priorities-next-chapter','Michael Fiddelke, Target''s new CEO, has unveiled four key priorities for the retailer''s future, focusing on merchandising authority, elevating guest experience, accelerating technology, and strengthening teams and communities. Fiddelke, who previously served as COO, was unanimously selected by Target''s board to succeed Brian Cornell. He aims to make clear choices, invest strategically, and implement this strategy through stores, digital experiences, and its people.','https://assets1.progressivegrocer.com/images/v/max_width_1440/files/2026-01/michael-fiddelke_target_2022_750x1000.jpg','Progressive Grocer','General','Progressive Grocer','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.941000"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.644823"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.606408"}]',0.335098,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.345654"}]','{"url": "https://progressivegrocer.com/new-target-ceo-outlines-4-priorities-next-chapter", "title": "New Target CEO Outlines 4 Priorities for Next Chapter", "source": "Progressive Grocer", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.941000"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.644823"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.606408"}], "authors": ["Emily Crowe"], "summary": "Michael Fiddelke, Target''s new CEO, has unveiled four key priorities for the retailer''s future, focusing on merchandising authority, elevating guest experience, accelerating technology, and strengthening teams and communities. Fiddelke, who previously served as COO, was unanimously selected by Target''s board to succeed Brian Cornell. He aims to make clear choices, invest strategically, and implement this strategy through stores, digital experiences, and its people.", "banner_image": "https://assets1.progressivegrocer.com/images/v/max_width_1440/files/2026-01/michael-fiddelke_target_2022_750x1000.jpg", "source_domain": "Progressive Grocer", "time_published": "20260202T154629", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.345654"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.335098}','2026-02-03 13:45:56',NULL),
	 (787,'alpha_vantage','TGT','TGT','2026-02-02 15:28:06','20260202T152806','New CEOs take reins at Walmart and Target facing much different scenarios','https://chainstoreage.com/new-ceos-take-reins-walmart-and-target-facing-much-different-scenarios','Walmart and Target have both appointed new CEOs, John Furner and Michael Fiddelke respectively, as of February 1st. Furner takes over Walmart at a time of strong financial performance and continues growth, while Fiddelke at Target faces significant challenges including an ongoing sales slump, messy stores, and pressure from consumer boycotts and social issues. Fiddelke has outlined a four-priority strategy to address these issues and improve the company''s performance.','https://assets1.chainstoreage.com/images/v/max_width_1440/2026-02/michael-fiddelke_target_2022_750x1000.jpg','Chain Store Age','General','Chain Store Age','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.733149"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.628281"}]',0.083986,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "WMT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.485145"}, {"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "0.995294", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.332095"}]','{"url": "https://chainstoreage.com/new-ceos-take-reins-walmart-and-target-facing-much-different-scenarios", "title": "New CEOs take reins at Walmart and Target facing much different scenarios", "source": "Chain Store Age", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.733149"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.628281"}], "authors": ["Marianne Wilson"], "summary": "Walmart and Target have both appointed new CEOs, John Furner and Michael Fiddelke respectively, as of February 1st. Furner takes over Walmart at a time of strong financial performance and continues growth,