	 (882,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-04 07:15:40','20260204T071540','Rep. David Taylor Purchases Shares of Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL)','https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/rep-david-taylor-purchases-shares-of-apple-inc-nasdaqaapl-2026-02-04/','Representative David Taylor (R-Ohio) recently purchased between $1,001 and $15,000 worth of Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) stock on January 16th and made several other trades on January 29th, buying Microsoft, Broadcom, Amazon, Salesforce, Prologis, Installed Building Products, and Medpace, while selling Amgen, Vertex, and Procter & Gamble. This news comes after Apple reported strong quarterly earnings, beating expectations with an EPS of $2.84 and revenue of $143.76 billion, leading analysts to maintain a "Moderate Buy" rating with an average price target of $291.70. The report also details Apple''s dividend announcement, stock performance metrics, and significant hedge fund activity, alongside mixed sentiment news regarding AI integration, talent drain, and supply chain concerns.','https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/apple-inc-logo-1200x675.png','MarketBeat','General','MarketBeat','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.949279"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.848855"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.833805"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.745914"}]',0.203176,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "AAPL", "relevance_score": "0.953256", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.497646"}, {"ticker": "MSFT", "relevance_score": "0.630331", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.233115"}, {"ticker": "AVGO", "relevance_score": "0.647922", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.142231"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.645863", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.202333"}, {"ticker": "CRM", "relevance_score": "0.646108", "ticker_sentiment_label":