	 (887,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-04 03:14:08','20260204T031408','Amazon Web Services CEO Says Space-Based Data Centers ''Not Economical'' Despite Jeff Bezos Pursuing The Idea','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/02/50362090/amazon-web-services-ceo-says-space-based-data-centers-not-economical-despite-jeff-bezos-pursuing-the-idea','The CEO of Amazon Web Services, Matt Garman, has stated that placing data centers in space is currently impractical and uneconomical, largely due to the high cost and logistical challenges of launching heavy equipment into orbit. This perspective stands despite the growing interest from tech giants like Amazon''s Blue Origin and Alphabet, which are exploring orbital data center concepts to meet increasing AI computing demands. Garman emphasizes that while space offers benefits like continuous solar power and easier cooling, the lack of sufficient rockets and the massive expense make it a long-term, rather than immediate, solution.','https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/02/03/Realistic-View-Of-The-Earth-From-Space--.jpeg?quality=85&auto=webp&width=850','Benzinga','General','Benzinga','[{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.926019"}]',0.00741,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.333324", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.010692"}]','{"url": "https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/02/50362090/amazon-web-services-ceo-says-space-based-data-centers-not-economical-despite-jeff-bezos-pursuing-the-idea", "title": "Amazon Web Services CEO Says Space-Based Data Centers ''Not Economical'' Despite Jeff Bezos Pursuing The Idea", "source": "Benzinga", "topics": [{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.926019"}], "authors": ["Ananya Gairola"], "summary": "The CEO of Amazon Web Services, Matt Garman, has stated that placing data centers in space is currently impractical and uneconomical, largely due to the high cost and logistical challenges of launching heavy equipment into orbit. This perspective stands despite the growing interest from tech giants like Amazon''s Blue Origin and Alphabet, which are exploring orbital data center concepts to meet increasing AI computing demands. Garman emphasizes that while space offers benefits like continuous solar power and easier cooling, the lack of sufficient rockets and the massive expense make it a long-term, rather than immediate, solution.", "banner_image": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/02/03/Realistic-View-Of-The-Earth-From-Space--.jpeg?quality=85&auto=webp&width=850", "source_domain": "Benzinga", "time_published": "20260204T031408", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.333324", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.010692"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.00741}','2026-02-04 12:45:54',NULL),
	 (888,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-04 02:58:49','20260204T025849','Spotify stock slides 7% below $500 — Checkout.com deal and Feb. 10 earnings keep SPOT in focus','https://ts2.tech/en/spotify-stock-slides-7-below-500-checkout-com-deal-and-feb-10-earnings-keep-spot-in-focus/','Spotify (SPOT) shares dropped nearly 7% following an expanded deal with Checkout.com for global payment processing, as investors anticipate its Q4 earnings report on February 10th. The upcoming earnings will be scrutinized for insights into the impact of recent price hikes, subscriber churn, and overall margins, with competition from tech giants adding to market pressures. The stock''s performance will be closely watched, particularly around the $464 support level.','https://ts2.tech/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/spotify-stock-slides-7-below-500-checkout-com-deal-and-feb-10-earnings-keep-spot-in-focus-featured.jpg','TechStock²','General','TechStock²','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.925095"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.830544"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.725551"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.622045"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.609570"}]',-0.125923,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "SPOT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.214422"}, {"ticker": "AAPL", "relevance_score": "0.641716", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.123192"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.606027", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.147895"}, {"ticker": "GOOGL", "relevance_score": "0.636163", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.108331"}]','{"url": "https://ts2.tech/en/spotify-stock-slides-7-below-500-checkout-com-deal-and-feb-10-earnings-keep-spot-in-focus/", "title": "Spotify stock slides 7% below $500 — Checkout.com deal and Feb. 10 earnings keep SPOT