	 (912,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-03 16:28:10','20260203T162810','Boom continues as Fabrinet posts 36% surge in sales revenues','https://optics.org/news/17/1/39','Fabrinet, a Bangkok-based contract manufacturer, announced record-breaking sales of $1.13 billion for the final quarter of 2025, a 36% increase year-over-year, driven by strong demand for photonics components in AI data centers. The company is significantly expanding its manufacturing capacity in Thailand and is focused on emerging technologies like co-packaged optics (CPO) and optical circuit switches (OCS) to sustain growth. Despite a recent dip in stock price due to geopolitical concerns, Fabrinet remains confident in continued sales boom.','https://optics.org/objects/news/thumb/17/1/39/FabrinetFebruary2026.jpg','Optics.org','General','Optics.org','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.944710"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.845939"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.801884"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.603525"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.611428"}]',0.467257,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "FN", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.886508"}, {"ticker": "NVDA", "relevance_score": "0.626211", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.317929"}, {"ticker": "CSCO", "relevance_score": "0.610876", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.348975"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.634774", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.315030"}, {"ticker": "GLW", "relevance_score": "0.597792", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.414382"}]','{"url": "https://optics.org/news/17/1/39", "title": "Boom continues as Fabrinet posts 36% surge in sales revenues", "source": "Optics.org", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.