	 (1012,'alpha_vantage','COST','COST','2026-02-03 16:42:19','20260203T164219','Costco pulls ‘no preservatives’ rotisserie chicken signs after additives lawsuit','https://ts2.tech/en/costco-pulls-no-preservatives-rotisserie-chicken-signs-after-additives-lawsuit/','Costco has removed "no preservatives" claims from its rotisserie chicken signs and online listings after a proposed class-action lawsuit alleged the claim was deceptive. Two California consumers argue the chicken contains sodium phosphate and carrageenan, which they say act as preservatives, despite Costco''s assertion that these are for moisture and texture. The lawsuit seeks class-action status for U.S. buyers, and Costco''s quick removal of the wording is seen by the plaintiffs'' attorney as an acknowledgment of the inaccuracy of their previous claims.','https://ts2.tech/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/costco-pulls-no-preservatives-rotisserie-chicken-signs-after-additives-lawsuit-featured.jpg','TechStock²','General','TechStock²','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.947863"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.707233"}]',-0.050817,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "COST", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.261925"}, {"ticker": "CAG", "relevance_score": "0.600631", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.146330"}, {"ticker": "KHC", "relevance_score": "0.645496", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.141746"}]','{"url": "https://ts2.tech/en/costco-pulls-no-preservatives-rotisserie-chicken-signs-after-additives-lawsuit/", "title": "Costco pulls ‘no preservatives’ rotisserie chicken signs after additives lawsuit", "source": "TechStock²", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.947863"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.707233"}], "authors": ["Shan Ahmed Khan"], "summary": "Costco has removed \\"no preservatives\\" claims from its rotisserie chicken signs and online listings after a proposed class-action lawsuit alleged the claim was deceptive. Two California consumers argue the chicken contains sodium phosphate and carrageenan, which they say act as preservatives, despite Costco''s assertion that these are for moisture and texture. The lawsuit seeks class-action status for U.S. buyers, and Costco''s quick removal of the wording is seen by the plaintiffs'' attorney as an acknowledgment of the inaccuracy of their previous claims.", "banner_image": "https://ts2.tech/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/costco-pulls-no-preservatives-rotisserie-chicken-signs-after-additives-lawsuit-featured.jpg", "source_domain": "TechStock²", "time_published": "20260203T164219", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "COST", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.261925"}, {"ticker": "CAG", "relevance_score": "0.600631", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.146330"}, {"ticker": "KHC", "relevance_score": "0.645496", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.141746"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": -0.050817}','2026-02-04 12:46:28',NULL),
	 (1013,'alpha_vantage','COST','COST','2026-02-03 16:28:07','20260203T162807','Dollar General Bets on Remodels as Its Next Growth Engine','https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/COST/pressreleases/37386526/dollar-general-bets-on-remodels-as-its-next-growth-engine/','Dollar General is shifting its growth strategy from new store openings to a strong focus on store remodels, particularly through its Project Elevate and Project Renovate programs, due to their attractive return profiles and lower capital intensity. The company plans for remodels to account for about 90% of its fiscal 2026 real estate projects alongside fewer new store openings, aiming to boost productivity and customer satisfaction in existing locations. Despite this shift, Dollar General''s shares have outperformed its industry and competitors like Costco and Target, and it holds a Zacks Rank #2 (Buy).','https://barchart-news-media-prod.aws.barchart.com/SYNDSRC/487af21bb9766d0a7604f15d942498d5/144681.jpg%3Fv%3D1840871139','The Globe and Mail','General','The Globe and Mail','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.898647"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.819841"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.658708"}]',0.132239,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "DG", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.418368"}, {"ticker": "COST", "relevance_score": "0.602331", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.114958"}, {"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "0.617730", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.217914"}]','{"url": "https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/COST/pressreleases/37386526/dollar-general-bets-on-remodels-as-its-next-growth-engine/", "title": "Dollar General Bets on Remodels as Its Next Growth Engine", "source": "The Globe and Mail", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.898647"}, {"topic": 