	 (1054,'alpha_vantage','TGT','DG','2026-02-03 16:28:07','20260203T162807','Dollar General Bets on Remodels as Its Next Growth Engine','https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/COST/pressreleases/37386526/dollar-general-bets-on-remodels-as-its-next-growth-engine/','Dollar General is shifting its growth strategy from new store openings to a strong focus on store remodels, particularly through its Project Elevate and Project Renovate programs, due to their attractive return profiles and lower capital intensity. The company plans for remodels to account for about 90% of its fiscal 2026 real estate projects alongside fewer new store openings, aiming to boost productivity and customer satisfaction in existing locations. Despite this shift, Dollar General''s shares have outperformed its industry and competitors like Costco and Target, and it holds a Zacks Rank #2 (Buy).','https://barchart-news-media-prod.aws.barchart.com/SYNDSRC/487af21bb9766d0a7604f15d942498d5/144681.jpg%3Fv%3D1840871139','The Globe and Mail','General','The Globe and Mail','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.898647"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.819841"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.658708"}]',0.132239,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "DG", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.418368"}, {"ticker": "COST", "relevance_score": "0.602331", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.114958"}, {"ticker": "TGT", "relevance_score": "0.617730", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.217914"}]','{"url": "https://www.theglobeandmail.com/investing/markets/stocks/COST/pressreleases/37386526/dollar-general-bets-on-remodels-as-its-next-growth-engine/", "title": "Dollar General Bets on Remodels as Its Next Growth Engine", "source": "The Globe and Mail", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.898647"}, {"topic": "ea