	 (1375,'alpha_vantage','CLX','CLX','2026-02-04 19:57:31','20260204T195731','Clorox Completes U.S, Canada ERP Upgrade','https://consumergoods.com/clorox-completes-us-canada-erp-upgrade','The Clorox Co. has successfully rolled out its new SAP-powered ERP system in the U.S. and Canada, a five-year, $580 million initiative designed to improve order management and manufacturing capabilities. This upgrade replaces a 20-year-old legacy system with a cloud-based structure, enabling integrated, real-time data sharing across finance, supply chain, and sales, leading to faster and more informed decisions. The company anticipates benefits including increased supplier collaboration, efficiency, expanded margins, and enhanced real-time insights for revenue growth management.','https://assets1.consumergoods.com/images/v/max_width_1440/2026-02/clorox_534139024.jpg','Consumer Goods Technology','General','Consumer Goods Technology','[{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.941296"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.733016"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.628382"}]',0.480646,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.492165"}]','{"url": "https://consumergoods.com/clorox-completes-us-canada-erp-upgrade", "title": "Clorox Completes U.S, Canada ERP Upgrade", "source": "Consumer Goods Technology", "topics": [{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.941296"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.733016"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.628382"}], "authors": ["Liz Dominguez"], "summary": "The Clorox Co. has successfully rolled out its new SAP-powered ERP system in the U.S. and Canada, a five-year, $580 million initiative designed to improve order management and manufacturing capabilities. This upgrade replaces a 20-year-old legacy system with a cloud-based structure, enabling integrated, real-time data sharing across finance, supply chain, and sales, leading to faster and more informed decisions. The company anticipates benefits including increased supplier collaboration, efficiency, expanded margins, and enhanced real-time insights for revenue growth management.", "banner_image": "https://assets1.consumergoods.com/images/v/max_width_1440/2026-02/clorox_534139024.jpg", "source_domain": "Consumer Goods Technology", "time_published": "20260204T195731", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.492165"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.480646}','2026-02-05 14:04:52',NULL),
	 (1376,'alpha_vantage','CLX','CLX','2026-02-04 16:38:08','20260204T163808','Is Clorox’s ERP Strain And GOJO Deal Altering The Investment Case For Clorox (CLX)?','https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/household/nyse-clx/clorox/news/is-cloroxs-erp-strain-and-gojo-deal-altering-the-investment','The Clorox Company''s investment narrative is currently shaped by ongoing ERP-related disruptions impacting margins and its recent acquisition of GOJO Industries. While sales were flat and EPS slipped in the latest quarter, management reaffirmed its full-year outlook, focusing on digital transformation, supply chain improvements, and innovation. The GOJO acquisition is intended to strengthen Clorox''s health and hygiene footprint but introduces additional integration risks at a time when ERP issues persist.',NULL,'Simply Wall Street','General','Simply Wall Street','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.946957"}, {"topic": "mergers_and_acquisitions", "relevance_score": "0.847579"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.743039"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.625953"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.605388"}]',-0.253167,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.285450"}]','{"url": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/household/nyse-clx/clorox/news/is-cloroxs-erp-strain-and-gojo-deal-altering-the-investment", "title": "Is Clorox’s ERP Strain And GOJO Deal Altering The Investment Case For Clorox (CLX)?", "source": "Simply Wall Street", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.946957"}, {"topic": "mergers_and_acquisitions", "relevance_score": "0.847579"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.743039"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.625953"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.605388"}], "authors": ["Simply Wall St", "Sasha Jovanovic"], "summary": "The Clorox Company''s investment narrative is currently shaped by ongoing ERP-related disruptions impacting margins and its recent acquisition of GOJO Industries. While sales were flat and EPS slipped in the latest quarter, management reaffirmed its full-year outlook, focusing on digital transformation, supply chain improvements, and innovation. The GOJO acquisition is intended to strengthen Clorox''s health and hygiene footprint but introduces additional integration risks at a time when ERP issues persist.", "banner_image": null, "source_domain": "Simply Wall Street", "time_published": "20260204T163808", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.285450"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "overall_sentiment_score": -0.253167}','2026-02-05 14:04:52',NULL),
	 (1380,'alpha_vantage','CLX','CLX','2026-02-04 15:14:54','20260204T151454','Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft Issues Pessimistic Forecast for Clorox (NYSE:CLX) Stock Price','https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/deutsche-bank-aktiengesellschaft-issues-pessimistic-forecast-for-clorox-nyseclx-stock-price-2026-02-04/','Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft has lowered its price target for Clorox (NYSE:CLX) from $114.00 to $112.00, maintaining a "hold" rating, which suggests a potential downside from its current price. This pessimistic forecast follows Clorox missing its Q2 earnings per share estimates, reporting $1.39 against a consensus of $1.43, and a warning of an inventory reset in 2026 that could further squeeze profits. Despite mixed analyst ratings, with an average "Reduce" recommendation and a consensus price target of $118.67, Clorox''s stock traded up on Wednesday, closing at $117.21.','https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/the-clorox-company-logo-1200x675.png?v=20250505090624','MarketBeat','General','MarketBeat','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.915753"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.922126"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.629616"}]',-0.139866,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "CLX", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.232536"}, {"ticker": "MS", "relevance_score": "0.643076", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.110800"}, {"ticker": "C", "relevance_score": "0.636703", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.128082"}, {"ticker": "WFC", "relevance_score": "0.617630", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.117822"}]','{"url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/deutsche-bank-aktiengesellschaft-issues-pessimistic-forecast-for-clorox-nyseclx-stock-price-2026-02-04/", "title": "Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft Issues Pessimistic Forecast for Clorox (NYSE:CLX) Stock Price",