	 (1383,'alpha_vantage','COLM','COLM','2026-02-04 23:28:49','20260204T232849','Columbia Sportswear Co (NASDAQ:COLM) Surges on Q4 Earnings Beat Despite Mixed Guidance','https://www.chartmill.com/news/COLM/Chartmill-41022-Columbia-Sportswear-Co-NASDAQCOLM-Surges-on-Q4-Earnings-Beat-Despite-Mixed-Guidance','Columbia Sportswear Co (COLM) reported strong Q4 2025 earnings, exceeding analyst expectations with EPS of $1.73 against an estimated $1.22, leading to a significant after-hours stock surge. While the company''s full-year 2026 sales forecast exceeded analyst estimates, its Q1 2026 outlook was cautious due to expected declines and tariff impacts. Investors reacted positively to the profitability and annual sales outlook, but near-term challenges remain.','https://www.chartmill.com/images/uploads/THUMBNAILS_CHARTMILL_1000_528_17_c249efcc18.webp','Chartmill','General','Chartmill','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.933820"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.846190"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.719714"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.628580"}]',0.418205,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "COLM", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.407329"}]','{"url": "https://www.chartmill.com/news/COLM/Chartmill-41022-Columbia-Sportswear-Co-NASDAQCOLM-Surges-on-Q4-Earnings-Beat-Despite-Mixed-Guidance", "title": "Columbia Sportswear Co (NASDAQ:COLM) Surges on Q4 Earnings Beat Despite Mixed Guidance", "source": "Chartmill", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.933820"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.846190"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.719714"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.628580"}], "authors": ["Mill Chart"], "summary": "Columbia Sportswear Co (COLM) reported strong Q4 2025 earnings, exceeding analyst expectations with EPS of $1.73 against an estimated $1.22, leading to a significant after-hours stock surge. While the company''s full-year 2026 sales forecast exceeded analyst estimates, its Q1 2026 outlook was cautious due to expected declines and tariff impacts. Investors reacted positively to the profitability and annual sales outlook, but near-term challenges remain.", "banner_image": "https://www.chartmill.com/images/uploads/THUMBNAILS_CHARTMILL_1000_528_17_c249efcc18.webp", "source_domain": "Chartmill", "time_published": "20260204T232849", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "COLM", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.407329"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.418205}','2026-02-05 14:04:54',NULL),
	 (1384,'alpha_vantage','COLM','COLM','2026-02-04 19:28:29','20260204T192829','US'' Columbia Sportswear posts 1% sales growth, margins improve in 2025','https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/company-news/apparel-news/us-columbia-sportswear-posts-1-sales-growth-margins-improve-in-2025-308180-newsdetails.htm','Columbia Sportswear reported a 1% net sales growth to $3.4 billion for the full year 2025, with improved gross margins despite tariff pressures and impairment charges impacting profits. While international growth was strong, Q4 sales declined, and the company forecasts modest revenue growth for 2026 but anticipates further margin pressure due to US tariffs and a softer outlook for Q1 earnings. The company maintains a strong balance sheet with no borrowings and significant cash holdings.','https://static.fibre2fashion.com/Newsresource/images/308/shutterstock-2437218015_319768.jpg','Fibre2Fashion','General','Fibre2Fashion','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.901581"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.817032"}, {"topic": "economy_fiscal", "relevance_score": "0.638947"}]',-0.288674,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "COLM", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.286865"}]','{"url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/company-news/apparel-news/us-columbia-sportswear-posts-1-sales-growth-margins-improve-in-2025-308180-newsdetails.htm", "title": "US'' Columbia Sportswear posts 1% sales growth, margins improve in 2025", "source": "Fibre2Fashion", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.901581"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.817032"}, {"topic": "economy_fiscal", "relevance_score": "0.638947"}], "authors": [], "summary": "Columbia Sportswear reported a 1% net sales growth to $3.4 billion for the full year 2025, with improved gross margins despite tariff pressures and impairment charges impacting profits. While international growth was strong, Q4