	 (1623,'alpha_vantage','TPR','TPR','2026-02-05 11:52:34','20260205T115234','Coach’s 25% Growth Powers Record Q2 Sales, Profits for Tapestry','https://wwd.com/business-news/financial/tapestry-q2-2025-earnings-coach-growth-1238539177/','Tapestry Inc. reported record second-quarter sales and profits, largely driven by Coach, which saw a 25% increase in sales to $2.1 billion. This strong performance led Tapestry to significantly raise its full-year outlook, with expected revenue growth of 11% to $7.75 billion and EPS rising over 25% to $6.40-$6.45. Despite a 14% sales decline at Kate Spade, Coach''s growth propelled overall revenue up 14% to $2.5 billion, and the company plans to return $1.5 billion to shareholders.','https://wwd.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/coach-spring-2026-backstage-NW-21.jpg?crop=0px%2C2px%2C1998px%2C1119px&resize=1000%2C563','WWD','General','WWD','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.928649"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.838188"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.629226"}]',0.80571,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "TPR", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.808631"}]','{"url": "https://wwd.com/business-news/financial/tapestry-q2-2025-earnings-coach-growth-1238539177/", "title": "Coach’s 25% Growth Powers Record Q2 Sales, Profits for Tapestry", "source": "WWD", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.928649"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.838188"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.629226"}], "authors": ["Evan Clark"], "summary": "Tapestry Inc. reported record second-quarter sales and profits, largely driven by Coach, which saw a 25% increase in sales to $2.1 billion. This strong performance led Tapestry to significantly raise its full-year outlook, with expected revenue growth of 11% to $7.75 billion and EPS rising over 25% to $6.40-$6.45. Despite a 14% sales decline at Kate Spade, Coach''s growth propelled overall revenue up 14% to $2.5 billion, and the company plans to return $1.5 billion to shareholders.", "banner_image": "https://wwd.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/coach-spring-2026-backstage-NW-21.jpg?crop=0px%2C2px%2C1998px%2C1119px&resize=1000%2C563", "source_domain": "WWD", "time_published": "20260205T115234", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "TPR", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.808631"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.80571}','2026-02-05 14:06:39',NULL),
	 (1624,'alpha_vantage','TPR','TPR','2026-02-05 11:50:34','20260205T115034','Tapestry (TPR) Tops Q2 EPS by 50c, Beats on Revenue; Offers FY26 Guidance','https://www.streetinsider.com/Earnings/Tapestry+%28TPR%29+Tops+Q2+EPS+by+50c%2C+Beats+on+Revenue%3B+Offers+FY26+Guidance/25950178.html','Tapestry (TPR) reported strong Q2 results, exceeding analyst expectations for both EPS and revenue. The company announced Q2 EPS of $2.69 against an estimate of $2.19, and revenue of $2.5 billion compared to the $2.29 billion consensus. Tapestry also provided its FY2026 guidance, projecting EPS between $5.45 and $5.60 and revenue of $7.75 billion, both surpassing consensus estimates with the revenue guidance.','https://www.streetinsider.com/images/summaries/1880/resize_Tapestry.jpg','StreetInsider','General','StreetInsider','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.805396"}]',0.51589,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "TPR", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.532365"}]','{"url": "https://www.streetinsider.com/Earnings/Tapestry+%28TPR%29+Tops+Q2+EPS+by+50c%2C+Beats+on+Revenue%3B+Offers+FY26+Guidance/25950178.html", "title": "Tapestry (TPR) Tops Q2 EPS by 50c, Beats on Revenue; Offers FY26 Guidance", "source": "StreetInsider", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.805396"}], "authors": [], "summary": "Tapestry (TPR) reported strong Q2 results, exceeding analyst expectations for both EPS and revenue. The company announced Q2 EPS of $2.69 against an estimate of $2.19, and revenue of $2.5 billion compared to the $2.29 billion consensus. Tapestry also provided its FY2026 guidance, projecting EPS between $5.45 and $5.60 and revenue of $7.75 billion, both surpassing consensus estimates with the revenue guidance.", "banner_image": "https://www.streetinsider.com/images/summaries/1880/resize_Tapestry.