	 (1649,'alpha_vantage','WMT','WMT','2026-02-05 10:49:21','20260205T104921','1 Bold Decision Helped Make Walmart a Trillion-Dollar Company. Most CEOs Do the Opposite','https://www.inc.com/minda-zetlin/1-bold-decision-helped-make-walmart-a-trillion-dollar-company-most-ceos-do-the-opposite/91297513','Walmart recently joined the exclusive group of companies valued at over $1 trillion, a significant achievement attributed largely to former CEO Doug McMillon. While many experts cite technology and AI as the main drivers, McMillon''s crucial decision to visit stores, listen to employees, and increase their pay was a foundational step that enabled these technological advancements. This bold move, which most CEOs would avoid, played a critical role in turning the company around from a challenging position when McMillon became CEO in 2014.','https://img-cdn.inc.com/image/upload/f_webp,c_fit,w_1920,q_auto/vip/2026/02/mcmillon-walmart-ceo-decision-inc.jpg','www.inc.com','General','www.inc.com','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.909377"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.830326"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.616797"}]',0.016189,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "WMT", "relevance_score": "0.320670", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.016220"}]','{"url": "https://www.inc.com/minda-zetlin/1-bold-decision-helped-make-walmart-a-trillion-dollar-company-most-ceos-do-the-opposite/91297513", "title": "1 Bold Decision Helped Make Walmart a Trillion-Dollar Company. Most CEOs Do the Opposite", "source": "www.inc.com", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.909377"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.830326"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.616797"}], "authors": ["MINDA ZETLIN"], "summary": "Walmart recently joined the exclusive group of companies valued at over $1 trillion, a significant achievement attributed largely to former CEO Doug McMillon. While many experts cite technology and AI as the main drivers, McMillon''s crucial decision to visit stores, listen to employees, and increase their pay was a foundational step that enabled these technological advancements. This bold move, which most CEOs would avoid, played a critical role in turning the company around from a challenging position when McMillon became CEO in 2014.", "banner_image": "https://img-cdn.inc.com/image/upload/f_webp,c_fit,w_1920,q_auto/vip/2026/02/mcmillon-walmart-ceo-decision-inc.jpg", "source_domain": "www.inc.com", "time_published": "20260205T104921", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "WMT", "relevance_score": "0.320670", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.016220"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.016189}','2026-02-05 14:06:56',NULL),
	 (1650,'alpha_vantage','WMT','WMT','2026-02-05 10:47:00','20260205T104700','SBI Securities Co. Ltd. Sells 2,828 Shares of Invesco QQQ $QQQ','https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-sbi-securities-co-ltd-sells-2828-shares-of-invesco-qqq-qqq-2026-02-05/','SBI Securities Co. Ltd. reduced its stake in Invesco QQQ by 1.4% in the third quarter, selling 2,828 shares but still holding 194,954 shares valued at $117 million, making it its sixth largest holding. The Invesco QQQ recently increased its quarterly dividend to $0.7941 per share, representing an annualized yield of approximately 0.5%. Institutional activity for QQQ shows a mixed picture, with some firms boosting holdings while others adjusted, and recent Nasdaq weakness and technical warnings suggest potential for further outflows.','https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/invesco-qqq-logo-1200x675.png?v=20231212200553','MarketBeat','General','MarketBeat','[{"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.927854"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.822686"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.746939"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.604670"}]',0.170607,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "IVZ", "relevance_score": "0.833278", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.045222"}, {"ticker": "JPM", "relevance_score": "0.642414", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.256846"}, {"ticker": "WMT", "relevance_score": "0.556271", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.096997"}, {"ticker": "NOW", "relevance_score": "0.551261", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.268906"}]','{"url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-sbi-securities-co-ltd-sells-2828-shares-of-invesco-qqq-qqq-2026-02-05/", "title": "SBI Securities Co. Ltd. Sells 2,828 Shares of Invesco QQQ $QQQ", "source": "MarketBeat", "topics": [{"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.92785