	 (1923,'alpha_vantage','PEP','PEP','2026-02-06 09:12:52','20260206T091252','AGF Management Ltd. Has $1.06 Million Position in PepsiCo, Inc. $PEP','https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-agf-management-ltd-has-106-million-position-in-pepsico-inc-pep-2026-02-06/','AGF Management Ltd. significantly reduced its stake in PepsiCo, Inc. by 70.2% in the third quarter, now holding 7,569 shares valued at approximately $1.063 million. This comes as PepsiCo reported strong Q4 results, surpassing analyst expectations with $2.26 EPS on $29.34 billion revenue, and reaffirmed its FY2026 guidance. The company''s board also approved a $10.0 billion share repurchase program and increased its quarterly dividend, reflecting a commitment to returning capital to shareholders.','https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/pepsico-inc-logo-1200x675.jpg?v=20210728083446','MarketBeat','General','MarketBeat','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.925798"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.817987"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.706400"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.617225"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.649219"}]',0.026304,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "0.318807", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.014907"}]','{"url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/instant-alerts/filing-agf-management-ltd-has-106-million-position-in-pepsico-inc-pep-2026-02-06/", "title": "AGF Management Ltd. Has $1.06 Million Position in PepsiCo, Inc. $PEP", "source": "MarketBeat", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.925798"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.817987"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.706400"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.617225"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.649219"}], "authors": ["MarketBeat"], "summary": "AGF Management Ltd. significantly reduced its stake in PepsiCo, Inc. by 70.2% in the third quarter, now holding 7,569 shares valued at approximately $1.063 million. This comes as PepsiCo reported strong Q4 results, surpassing analyst expectations with $2.26 EPS on $29.34 billion revenue, and reaffirmed its FY2026 guidance. The company''s board also approved a $10.0 billion share repurchase program and increased its quarterly dividend, reflecting a commitment to returning capital to shareholders.", "banner_image": "https://www.marketbeat.com/logos/pepsico-inc-logo-1200x675.jpg?v=20210728083446", "source_domain": "MarketBeat", "time_published": "20260206T091252", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "0.318807", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.014907"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.026304}','2026-02-06 12:40:41',NULL),
	 (1924,'alpha_vantage','PEP','PEP','2026-02-05 20:15:09','20260205T201509','PepsiCo reports $93.9B revenues for 2025, profit $11.5B','https://westfaironline.com/earnings/pepsico-reports-93-9b-revenues-for-2025-profit-11-5b/','PepsiCo, Inc. reported full-year revenues of $93.9 billion for 2025, an increase from $91.9 billion in 2024, though operating profit decreased to $11.5 billion from $12.9 billion. The company announced a 54th consecutive increase in its annualized stock dividend to $5.92 per share and a plan to repurchase up to $10 billion of common stock. Additionally, PepsiCo is cutting prices on many snack products by 15% and reducing its U.S. product offerings by 20%.','https://westfaironline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Pepsico-logo.png','Westfair Communications','General','Westfair Communications','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.943102"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.802978"}]',0.295894,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.276000"}]','{"url": "https://westfaironline.com/earnings/pepsico-reports-93-9b-revenues-for-2025-profit-11-5b/", "title": "PepsiCo reports $93.9B revenues for 2025, profit $11.5B", "source": "Westfair Communications", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.943102"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.802978"}], "authors": ["Peter Katz"], "summary": "PepsiCo, Inc. reported full-year revenues of $93.9 billion for 2025, an increase from $91.9 billion in 2024, though operating profit decreased to $11.5 billion from $12.9 billion. The company announced a 54th consecutive increase in its annualized stock dividend to $5.92 per share and a plan to repurchase up to $10 billion of common stock. Additionally, PepsiCo is cutting prices on many snack products by 15% and reducing its U.S. product offerings by 20%.", "banner_image": "https://westfaironline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Pepsico-logo.png", "source_domain": "Westfair Communications", "time_published": "20260205T201509", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.276000"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.295894}','2026-02-06 12:40:41',NULL),
	 (1931,'alpha_vantage','PEP','PEP','2026-02-05 14:29:17','20260205T142917','PepsiCo preparing for GLP-1 opportunity','https://www.bakingbusiness.com/articles/65607-pepsico-preparing-for-glp-1-opportunity','PepsiCo is strategically preparing for the widespread adoption of GLP-1 medications for weight loss by focusing on opportunities rather than threats. The company plans to leverage portion control, hydration, fiber, and protein in its product development. This includes innovations like Pepsi Prebiotic cola, Gatorade Lower Sugar, and various Muscle Milk and Starbucks protein offerings, aiming to capitalize on these new consumer needs across multiple markets.','https://www.bakingbusiness.com/ext/resources/2025/10/30/SSW-Trends-Lead_Pepsico.webp?height=667&t=1761908736&width=1080','Baking Business','General','Baking Business','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.817322"}, {"topic": "life_sciences", "relevance_score": "0.739992"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.647068"}]',0.441543,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.438044"}]','{"url": "https://www.bakingbusiness.com/articles/65607-pepsico-preparing-for-glp-1-opportunity", "title": "PepsiCo preparing for GLP-1 opportunity", "source": "Baking Business", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.817322"}, {"topic": "life_sciences", "relevance_score": "0.739992"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.647068"}], "authors": ["By Keith Nunes"], "summary": "PepsiCo is strategically preparing for the widespread adoption of GLP-1 medications for weight loss by focusing on opportunities rather than threats. The company plans to leverage portion control, hydration, fiber, and protein in its product development. This includes innovations like Pepsi Prebiotic cola, Gatorade Lower Sugar, and various Muscle Milk and Starbucks protein offerings, aiming to capitalize on these new consumer needs across multiple markets.", "banner_image": "https://www.bakingbusiness.com/ext/resources/2025/10/30/SSW-Trends-Lead_Pepsico.webp?height=667&t=1761908736&width=1080", "source_domain": "Baking Business", "time_published": "20260205T142917", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.438044"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.441543}','2026-02-06 12:40:41',NULL),
	 (1932,'alpha_vantage','PEP','PEP','2026-02-05 14:25:00','20260205T142500','UBS Lifts PepsiCo (PEP) Target After Solid Q4 Execution','https://finviz.com/news/301963/ubs-lifts-pepsico-pep-target-after-solid-q4-execution','UBS analyst Peter Grom raised the price target for PepsiCo (PEP) to $190 from $170, reiterating a Buy rating, following strong Q4 execution and reiterated 2026 outlook. PepsiCo plans strategic price cuts on snack brands and is focusing on portion control and healthier options across its portfolio to adjust to changing consumer behavior, including the impact of weight-loss drugs and budget constraints. Despite these adjustments, the company aims to restore volume growth in North America snacks.','https://d2gr5kl7dt2z3t.cloudfront.net/blog/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/05081842/ja-san-miguel-xYSp0kkIUio-unsplash.jpg','Finviz','General','Finviz','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.932755"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.830347"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.712896"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.635120"}]',0.320353,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "PEP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.319792"}]','{"url": "https://finviz.com/news/301963/ubs-lifts-pepsico-pep-target-after-solid-q4-execution", "title": "UBS Lifts PepsiCo (PEP) Target After Solid Q4 Execution", "source": "Finviz", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.932755"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.830347"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.712896"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.635120"}], "authors": ["Vardah Gill"], "summary": "UBS analyst Peter Grom raised the price target for PepsiCo (PEP) to $190 from $170, reiterating a Buy rating, following strong Q4 execution and reiterated 2026 outlook. PepsiCo plans strategic price cuts on snack brands and is focusing on portion co