	 (1939,'alpha_vantage','PG','PG','2026-02-05 16:58:29','20260205T165829','Procter & Gamble Up 1%. Analysts Point to $200 Valuation Case','https://www.tikr.com/blog/procter-gamble-up-1-analysts-points-to-200-valuation-case','Procter & Gamble (PG) stock rose 1% last week despite management commentary indicating a soft Q2 FY2026 and slower U.S. volume growth. Analysts see a valuation case for PG reaching $200, with a valuation model suggesting the stock is currently undervalued relative to a $202.26 target price over 2.4 years. This assessment is based on projected 3% revenue growth, 25.7% operating margins, and a 23x exit P/E multiple.','https://res.cloudinary.com/tikr/images/f_auto,q_auto,w_800/v1770304894/images/FEATURED-IMAGE-MAKER-159/FEATURED-IMAGE-MAKER-159','TIKR.com','General','TIKR.com','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.912115"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.818828"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.632514"}]',0.111613,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "PG", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.125873"}]','{"url": "https://www.tikr.com/blog/procter-gamble-up-1-analysts-points-to-200-valuation-case", "title": "Procter & Gamble Up 1%. Analysts Point to $200 Valuation Case", "source": "TIKR.com", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.912115"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.818828"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.632514"}], "authors": ["Gian Estrada", "Thomas Richmond"], "summary": "Procter & Gamble (PG) stock rose 1% last week despite management commentary indicating a soft Q2 FY2026 and slower U.S. volume growth. Analysts see a valuation case for PG reaching $200, with a valuation model suggesting the stock is currently undervalued relative to a $202.26 target price over 2.4 years. This assessment is based on projected 3% revenue growth, 25.7% operating margins, and a 23x exit P/E multiple.", "ba