	 (2260,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-06 17:34:16','20260206T173416','Coca-Cola shifting sports drink business BodyArmor to Atlanta, report says','https://www.ajc.com/business/2026/02/coca-cola-shifting-sports-drink-business-bodyarmor-to-atlanta-report-says/','Coca-Cola is reportedly moving its BodyArmor Sports Nutrition business from New York to Atlanta, integrating it into a new unit that will also include Powerade, Vitaminwater, and Smartwater. This consolidation aims to streamline operations and enhance consistency across its hydration brands. Coca-Cola fully acquired BodyArmor in 2021 for $5.6 billion, adding to its portfolio which already features leading sports drink brands like Powerade.','https://images.ajc.com/resizer/v2/7HZ2VZJ5QLDZONTXFL2DKOFFNU.jpg?auth=9a9790d23c10caead9a0a09e05f6b970634629ab0cf2c62c4a93c726353d5a7d&width=1280&height=720&smart=true','AJC.com','General','AJC.com','[{"topic": "mergers_and_acquisitions", "relevance_score": "0.905558"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.832350"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.607208"}]',0.219201,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.203419"}]','{"url": "https://www.ajc.com/business/2026/02/coca-cola-shifting-sports-drink-business-bodyarmor-to-atlanta-report-says/", "title": "Coca-Cola shifting sports drink business BodyArmor to Atlanta, report says", "source": "AJC.com", "topics": [{"topic": "mergers_and_acquisitions", "relevance_score": "0.905558"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.832350"}, {"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.607208"}], "authors": ["Amy Wenk"], "summary": "Coca-Cola is reportedly moving its BodyArmor Sports Nutrition business from New York to Atlanta, integrating it into a new unit that will also include Powerade, Vitaminwater, and Smartwater. This consolidation aims to streamline operations and enhance consistency across its hydration brands. Coca-Cola fully acquired BodyArmor in 2021 for $5.6 billion, adding to its portfolio which already features leading sports drink brands like Powerade.", "banner_image": "https://images.ajc.com/resizer/v2/7HZ2VZJ5QLDZONTXFL2DKOFFNU.jpg?auth=9a9790d23c10caead9a0a09e05f6b970634629ab0cf2c62c4a93c726353d5a7d&width=1280&height=720&smart=true", "source_domain": "AJC.com", "time_published": "20260206T173416", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.203419"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.219201}','2026-02-07 13:35:14',NULL),
	 (2261,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-06 17:32:16','20260206T173216','Shifting tastes freeze out Minute Maid as Coca-Cola discontinues frozen concentrate cans','https://ktxs.com/news/nation-world/shifting-tastes-freeze-out-minute-maid-as-coca-cola-ditches-frozen-concentrate-cans-orange-juice-lemonade-limeade-breakfast-beverages-drinks-citrus-protein-shakes-smoothies','Coca-Cola is discontinuing its Minute Maid frozen juice concentrates in the U.S. and Canada, including orange juice, lemonade, and limeade, due to shifting consumer preferences towards fresh, ready-to-drink beverages. This move comes 80 years after Minute Maid first introduced frozen concentrate, as sales have declined over decades, partly due to rising citrus prices and consumer skepticism about sugary drinks. The company expects existing supplies to last until April.','https://ktxs.com/resources/media2/16x9/3225/986/0x211/90/67a0addd-933c-4e86-8836-87f619ccc36c-AP26035821817136.jpg','KTXS','General','KTXS','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.831738"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.648717"}]',0.143404,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.139007"}]','{"url": "https://ktxs.com/news/nation-world/shifting-tastes-freeze-out-minute-maid-as-coca-cola-ditches-frozen-concentrate-cans-orange-juice-lemonade-limeade-breakfast-beverages-drinks-citrus-protein-shakes-smoothies", "title": "Shifting tastes freeze out Minute Maid as Coca-Cola discontinues frozen concentrate cans", "source": "KTXS", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.831738"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.648717"}], "authors": ["JESSICA A. BOTELHO"], "summary": "Coca-Cola is discontinuing its Minute Maid frozen juice concentrates in the U.S. and Canada, including orange juice, lemonade, and limeade, due to shifting consumer preferences towards fresh, ready-to-drink beverages. This move comes 80 years after Minute Maid first introduced frozen concentrate, as sales have declined over decades, partly due to rising citrus prices and consumer skepticism about sugary drinks. The company expects existing supplies to last until April.", "banner_image": "https://ktxs.com/resources/media2/16x9/3225/986/0x211/90/67a0addd-933c-4e86-8836-87f619ccc36c-AP26035821817136.jpg", "source_domain": "KTXS", "time_published": "20260206T173216", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.139007"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.143404}','2026-02-07 13:35:14',NULL),
	 (2262,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-06 14:57:24','20260206T145724','Coca-Cola ends Minute Maid frozen juice after 80 years','https://rollingout.com/2026/02/06/coca-cola-minute-maid-shutdown/','Coca-Cola is discontinuing its Minute Maid frozen juice concentrates after 80 years, reflecting a shift in consumer preferences towards ready-to-drink options. This decision removes a budget-friendly and iconic kitchen staple, forcing consumers towards more expensive alternatives and introducing financial pressure, particularly for budget-conscious households. While Coca-Cola aims to cater to the demand for convenience, this move signifies the end of a product that offered an economical and accessible way to consume juice for generations.','https://rollingout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/shutterstock_2180620731-768x512.jpg','Rolling Out','General','Rolling Out','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.836768"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.714608"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.640921"}]',0.107242,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.104746"}]','{"url": "https://rollingout.com/2026/02/06/coca-cola-minute-maid-shutdown/", "title": "Coca-Cola ends Minute Maid frozen juice after 80 years", "source": "Rolling Out", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.836768"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.714608"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.640921"}], "authors": ["Shekari Philemon"], "summary": "Coca-Cola is discontinuing its Minute Maid frozen juice concentrates after 80 years, reflecting a shift in consumer preferences towards ready-to-drink options. This decision removes a budget-friendly and iconic kitchen staple, forcing consumers towards more expensive alternatives and introducing financial pressure, particularly for budget-conscious households. While Coca-Cola aims to cater to the demand for convenience, this move signifies the end of a product that offered an economical and accessible way to consume juice for generations.", "banner_image": "https://rollingout.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/shutterstock_2180620731-768x512.jpg", "source_domain": "Rolling Out", "time_published": "20260206T145724", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.104746"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.107242}','2026-02-07 13:35:14',NULL),
	 (2263,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-06 14:21:48','20260206T142148','Coca-Cola discontinues frozen juice can product category','https://www.kioskmarketplace.com/news/coca-cola-discontinues-frozen-juice-can-product-category/','Coca-Cola, through its Minute Maid brand, is discontinuing its frozen juice concentrate product category. This decision is attributed to a shift in consumer preferences, as the company aims to focus on products that better align with current demand. The Minute Maid frozen juices had a long history, first introduced in 1946 by Vacuum Foods Corporation, which Coca-Cola acquired in 1960.','https://nmgprod.s3.amazonaws.com/media/file/a2/a6/8078a1b45df4ae968a04a9de7d6a/cover_image__U9skBJcC__AdobeStock_431022699_Editorial_U.jpeg.960x540_q85_crop_upscale.jpg','Kiosk Marketplace','General','Kiosk Marketplace','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.842348"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.627055"}]',-0.182948,'Somewhat-Bearish','[{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.171439"}]','{"url": "https://www.kioskmarketplace.com/news/coca-cola-discontinues-frozen-juice-can-product-category/", "title": "Coca-Cola discontinues frozen juice can product category", "source": "Kiosk Marketplace", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.842348"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.627055"}], "authors": [], "summary": "Coca-Cola, through its Minute Maid brand, is discontinuing its frozen juice concentrate product category. This decision is attributed to a shift in consumer preferences, as the company aims to focus on products that better align with current demand. The Minute Maid frozen juices had a long history, first introduced in 1946 by Vacuum Foods Corporation, which Coca-Cola acquired in 1960.", "banner_image": "https://nmgprod.s3.amazonaws.com/media/file/a2/a6/8078a1b45df4ae968a04a9de7d6a/cover_image__U