	 (2344,'alpha_vantage','ROST','ROST','2026-02-07 05:08:56','20260207T050856','Some Good Fashion Cents: Boys and Girls Clubs of America, Ross Stores join forces for fundraiser','https://www.newsandsentinel.com/news/business/2026/02/some-good-fashion-cents-boys-and-girls-clubs-of-america-ross-stores-join-forces-for-fundraiser/','Ross Stores, Inc. is partnering with the Boys & Girls Clubs of America for its 12th annual "Help Local Kids Succeed in School" fundraiser. The campaign, running from February 7th to March 1st, encourages customers to donate at checkout at Ross Dress for Less stores, with all proceeds benefiting the Power Hour homework help and tutoring program. The Ross Stores Foundation will match donations up to $500,000 to further support the initiative.','https://ogden_images.s3.amazonaws.com/www.newsandsentinel.com/images/2026/02/06223604/02-07-26-Ross-1-tle-400x300.jpg','News and Sentinel','General','News and Sentinel','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.827423"}]',0.541643,'Bullish','[{"ticker": "ROST", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.538576"}]','{"url": "https://www.newsandsentinel.com/news/business/2026/02/some-good-fashion-cents-boys-and-girls-clubs-of-america-ross-stores-join-forces-for-fundraiser/", "title": "Some Good Fashion Cents: Boys and Girls Clubs of America, Ross Stores join forces for fundraiser", "source": "News and Sentinel", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.827423"}], "authors": ["Staff Reports"], "summary": "Ross Stores, Inc. is partnering with the Boys & Girls Clubs of America for its 12th annual \\"Help Local Kids Succeed in School\\" fundraiser. The campaign, running from February 7th to March 1st, encourages customers to donate at checkout at Ross Dress for Less stores, with all proceeds benefiting the Power Hour homework help and tutoring program. The Ross Stores Foundation will match donations up to $500,000 to further support the initiative.", "banner_image": "https://ogden_images.s3.amazonaws.com/www.newsandsentinel.com/images/2026/02/06223604/02-07-26-Ross-1-tle-400x300.jpg", "source_domain": "News and Sentinel", "time_published": "20260207T050856", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "ROST", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.538576"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.541643}','2026-02-07 13:35:58',NULL),
	 (2345,'alpha_vantage','SFM','SFM','2026-02-06 16:58:39','20260206T165839','P/E Ratio Insights for Sprouts Farmers Market','https://www.benzinga.com/insights/news/26/02/50453572/pe-ratio-insights-for-sprouts-farmers-market','Sprouts Farmers Market (NASDAQ: SFM) saw a 2.22% price spike, reaching $66.40, though its stock fell 12.14% last month and 59.84% over the past year. The article analyzes SFM''s Price-to-Earnings (P/E) ratio, noting it is lower than the Consumer Staples Distribution & Retail industry average, potentially indicating undervaluation. It concludes that while P/E is a useful metric, it should be considered alongside other factors like industry trends and business cycles for informed investment decisions.','https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/1770397221_0.png?optimize=medium&dpr=2&auto=webp&width=1920','Benzinga','General','Benzinga','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.936458"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.833610"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.742471"}]',0.026242,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "SFM", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.038082"}]','{"url": "https://www.benzinga.com/insights/news/26/02/50453572/pe-ratio-insights-for-sprouts-farmers-market", "title": "P/E Ratio Insights for Sprouts Farmers Market", "source": "Benzinga", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.936458"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.833610"}, {"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.742471"}], "authors": ["Benzinga Insights", "Benzinga Staff Writer"], "summary": "Sprouts Farmers Market (NASDAQ: SFM) saw a 2.22% price spike, reaching $66.40, though its stock fell 12.14% last month and 59.84% over the past year. The article analyzes SFM''s Price-to-Earnings (P/E) ratio, noting it is lower than the Consumer Staples Distribution & Retail industry average, potentially indicating undervaluation. It conclud