	 (2495,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-07 17:33:59','20260207T173359','Coca-Cola strikes ''crucial'' partnership that will be game-changer for its products: ''Making great progress''','https://www.thecooldown.com/green-business/coca-cola-mexico-recycling-plant-expansion/','Coca-Cola Mexico and PetStar have partnered to expand a food-grade PET recycling plant in Toluca, Mexico, investing $141.7 million to significantly boost its recycling capacity to 123,000 tons of PET waste annually. This expansion aims to transform waste into a resource, neutralize the carbon footprint, and make progress towards water neutrality, supporting the circular economy despite Coca-Cola''s status as a major contributor to plastic waste. The initiative aligns with Mexico''s new General Law on Circular Economy, emphasizing the country''s commitment to sustainable practices.','https://www.thecooldown.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Coca-Cola-Mexicoimage-rec03QO8bae9bULRe-1.jpg','The Cool Down','General','The Cool Down','[{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.811349"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.743658"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.602318"}]',0.315615,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.342638"}]','{"url": "https://www.thecooldown.com/green-business/coca-cola-mexico-recycling-plant-expansion/", "title": "Coca-Cola strikes ''crucial'' partnership that will be game-changer for its products: ''Making great progress''", "source": "The Cool Down", "topics": [{"topic": "retail_wholesale", "relevance_score": "0.811349"}, {"topic": "manufacturing", "relevance_score": "0.743658"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.602318"}], "authors": ["Matthew Swigonski"], "summary": "Coca-Cola Mexico and PetStar have partnered to expand a food-grade PET recycling plant in Toluca, Mexico, investing $141.7 million to significantly boost its recycling capacity to 123,000 tons of PET waste annually. This expansion aims to transform waste into a resource, neutralize the carbon footprint, and make progress towards water neutrality, supporting the circular economy despite Coca-Cola''s status as a major contributor to plastic waste. The initiative aligns with Mexico''s new General Law on Circular Economy, emphasizing the country''s commitment to sustainable practices.", "banner_image": "https://www.thecooldown.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Coca-Cola-Mexicoimage-rec03QO8bae9bULRe-1.jpg", "source_domain": "The Cool Down", "time_published": "20260207T173359", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.342638"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.315615}','2026-02-08 12:10:53',NULL),
	 (2496,'alpha_vantage','KO','KO','2026-02-07 13:28:54','20260207T132854','Keurig Dr Pepper (NASDAQ:KDP) Has Announced A Dividend Of $0.23','https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/food-beverage-tobacco/nasdaq-kdp/keurig-dr-pepper/news/keurig-dr-pepper-nasdaqkdp-has-announced-a-dividend-of-023','Keurig Dr Pepper (NASDAQ:KDP) has declared a dividend of $0.23 per share, payable on April 10th, resulting in a 3.2% yield. While the dividend currently makes up a significant portion of earnings and cash flow, future EPS growth is projected to make the payout ratio more comfortable. However, the article expresses caution regarding the sustainability and growth prospects of the dividend due to its relatively short history and slow earnings growth.','https://images.simplywall.st/news/images/blue-bear.svg','Simply Wall Street','General','Simply Wall Street','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.935401"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.710131"}]',-0.102297,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "KDP", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.269735"}, {"ticker": "MNST", "relevance_score": "0.611254", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.005378"}, {"ticker": "KO", "relevance_score": "0.607249", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.022527"}]','{"url": "https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/food-beverage-tobacco/nasdaq-kdp/keurig-dr-pepper/news/keurig-dr-pepper-nasdaqkdp-has-announced-a-dividend-of-023", "title": "Keurig Dr Pepper (NASDAQ:KDP) Has Announced A Dividend Of $0.23", "source": "Simply Wall Street", "topics": [{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.935401"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.710131"}], "authors": ["Simply Wall St"], "summary": "Keurig Dr Pepper (NASDAQ:KDP) has declared a dividend of $0.23 per share, payable on April 10th, resulting in a 3.2% yield. While the dividend currently makes up a significant portion