	 (2540,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-08 19:58:10','20260208T195810','Applied Materials stock jumped 6% Friday — here’s what could move AMAT next week','https://ts2.tech/en/applied-materials-stock-jumped-6-friday-heres-what-could-move-amat-next-week/','Applied Materials (AMAT) stock rose 6.09% on Friday, closing at $322.51, following a broader chip surge driven by increased capital expenditure plans from Amazon and Alphabet and strong AI chip demand. Investors are now looking forward to Applied Materials'' fiscal first-quarter report on February 12th, with attention focused on management''s views on chipmakers'' factory spending and potential impacts from U.S. export controls on its China business. Macroeconomic factors like the U.S. jobs report and CPI data, delayed by a federal government shutdown, along with Federal Reserve commentary, could also influence the stock''s performance.','https://ts2.tech/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/applied-materials-stock-jumped-6-friday-heres-what-could-move-amat-next-week-featured.jpg','TechStock²','General','TechStock²','[{"topic": "earnings", "relevance_score": "0.929754"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.947074"}, {"topic": "economy_monetary", "relevance_score": "0.748385"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.800077"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.939752"}]',0.242514,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "AMAT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.254815"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.767073", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.329214"}, {"ticker": "GOOGL", "relevance_score": "0.694963", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.275700"}, {"ticker": "LRCX", "relevance_score": "0.636785", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.204561"}, {"ticker": "SNPS", "relevance_score": "0.609903", "t