r top stock picks. Bryn Talkington chose Horizon Kinetics Inflation Beneficiaries ETF, Stephen Weiss selected Amazon.com, Jim Lebenthal picked Transocean Ltd., and Joe Terranova suggested Interactive Brokers Group, Inc. The article also provides recent financial performance details for Amazon, Transocean, and Interactive Brokers.", "banner_image": "https://cdn.benzinga.com/files/images/story/2026/02/10/Two-Diverse-Crypto-Traders-Brokers-Stock.jpeg?quality=85&auto=webp&width=850", "source_domain": "Benzinga", "time_published": "20260210T132457", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.968236", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.134916"}], "category_within_source": "General", "overall_sentiment_label": "Neutral", "overall_sentiment_score": 0.111216}','2026-02-10 15:55:10',NULL),
	 (2703,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-10 12:50:08','20260210T125008','Gartner: European spending on sovereign cloud IaaS to nearly double in 2026','https://www.computerworld.com/article/4129552/gartner-european-spending-on-sovereign-cloud-iaas-to-nearly-double-in-2026.html','European organizations are projected to nearly double their spending on sovereign cloud Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) in 2026, reaching $12.6 billion, due to geopolitical tensions and a desire to reduce reliance on US hyperscalers. This trend, termed "geopatriation," will see businesses moving existing workloads to local cloud providers, posing a challenge for hyperscalers who must adapt to avoid losing market share. While US-owned "sovereign" cloud services exist, their true sovereignty is questioned, suggesting partnerships with local providers might be a better approach for hyperscalers.','https://www.computerworld.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/4129552-0-53130100-1770727616-tim-mossholder-9B3xYEhxGQc-unsplash.jpg?quality=50&strip=all&w=1024','Computerworld','General','Computerworld','[{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.706714"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.638176"}]',-0.10818,'Neutral','[{"ticker": "IT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.293088"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.730356", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.247514"}, {"ticker": "MSFT", "relevance_score": "0.713249", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.230705"}, {"ticker": "GOOGL", "relevance_score": "0.662896", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.220034"}, {"ticker": "ORCL", "relevance_score": "0.637262", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.158043"}]','{"url": "https://www.computerworld.com/article/4129552/gartner-european-spending-on-sovereign-cloud-iaas-to-nearly-double-in-2026.html", "title": "Gartner: European spending on sovereign cloud IaaS to nearly double in 2026", "source": "Computerworld", "topics": [{"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "1.000000"}, {"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.706714"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.638176"}], "authors": ["Matthew Finnegan"], "summary": "European organizations are projected to nearly double their spending on sovereign cloud Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) in 2026, reaching $12.6 billion, due to geopolitical tensions and a desire to reduce reliance on US hyperscalers. This trend, termed \\"geopatriation,\\" will see businesses moving existing workloads to local cloud providers, posing a challenge for hyperscalers who must adapt to avoid losing market share. While US-owned \\"sovereign\\" cloud services exist, their true sovereignty is questioned, suggesting partnerships with local providers might be a better approach for hyperscalers.", "banner_image": "https://www.computerworld.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/4129552-0-53130100-1770727616-tim-mossholder-9B3xYEhxGQc-unsplash.jpg?quality=50&strip=all&w=1024", "source_domain": "Computerworld", "time_published": "20260210T125008", "ticker_sentiment": [{"ticker": "IT", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.293088"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.730356", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.247514"}, {"ticker": "MSFT", "relevance_score": "0.713249", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.230705"}, {"ticker": "GOOGL", "relevance_score": "0.662896", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "-0.220034"}, {"ticker": "ORCL", "relevance_score": "0.637262", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bearish", "ticker_sentiment_score": 