	 (2718,'alpha_vantage','AMZN','AMZN','2026-02-09 21:59:18','20260209T215918','Freedom Holding Corp. Eyes U.S. Debt Market to Fund Telecom and Data Center Expansion','https://riverjournalonline.com/business/freedom-holding-corp-eyes-u-s-debt-market-to-fund-telecom-and-data-center-expansion/289090/','Freedom Holding Corp., led by Kazakhstani billionaire Timur Turlov, is considering entering the U.S. debt market to raise $300-500 million for expanding its telecom infrastructure and building data centers. This move aims to fund large-scale investment in digital infrastructure to provide cloud services to major tech companies, government institutions, and private businesses, shifting the group''s strategy towards a more capital-intensive, infrastructure-based business model. Turlov emphasizes the importance of building long-term relationships with U.S. investors and the strategic integration into the global capital market, while also exploring international expansion for its Superapp.','https://riverjournalonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Freedom-Corp-300x169.png','River Journal Online','General','River Journal Online','[{"topic": "financial_markets", "relevance_score": "0.829590"}, {"topic": "technology", "relevance_score": "0.808077"}, {"topic": "finance", "relevance_score": "0.732024"}, {"topic": "mergers_and_acquisitions", "relevance_score": "0.633057"}, {"topic": "economy_macro", "relevance_score": "0.621584"}]',0.251928,'Somewhat-Bullish','[{"ticker": "FRHC", "relevance_score": "1.000000", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.403711"}, {"ticker": "AMZN", "relevance_score": "0.624286", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.349257"}, {"ticker": "MSFT", "relevance_score": "0.640854", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.341607"}, {"ticker": "NVDA", "relevance_score": "0.626281", "ticker_sentiment_label": "Somewhat-Bullish", "ticker_sentiment_score": "0.337165"